  "label": "Flow Matching Single Cell Dynamics",
  "related": [
    "multi-omics-760a",
    "classification-multi-b0d7",
    "transcription-ipsc-7c87"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [
    "single-cell"
  ],
  "slug": "networks-expression-d5f5",
  "summary": "Benchmarks show perturbation models degrade out-of-distribution, while flow-matching variants extend to trajectory and fate inference.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is generative flow-matching and dynamical modeling applied to single-cell data. SynGeneFlow learns non-additive residuals over an additive prior for perturbation response, and GeoSinkhorn Flow adds perturbation conditioning and geometry-aware transport to static phenoscapes. LoCoFlow and LineageFlow use local point-cloud geometry, conditional fate uncertainty, and growth correction to infer trajectories and clonal fate distributions. DCAF pairs data reconstruction and log-fold-change evaluation with JEPA-based regulatory modeling. A counterweight is EL-PERTURB, which finds that performance of twenty perturbation prediction models degrades out-of-distribution on Perturb-seq screens. Related items extend representation learning to spatial transcriptomics (Tessera), lineage inference from heritable memory genes (isCORAL), and causal state-transition decomposition (CauTrigger). What is new is the coupling of transport geometry with explicit growth and fate uncertainty, though most items are preprints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-24"
}
